def all_unique(lst):
    """Return True if all elements in the list are unique, otherwise False."""
    return len(lst) == len(set(lst))
```

This works by converting the list to a set, which removes duplicate values. If the lengths of the set and the original list match, every element was unique. Note that this requires the elements to be hashable; for unhashable items (such as lists), a different approach would be needed.

